module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.seed_fold_accumulator_declared_from_an_open_init

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { AwaitsOneGrounding, GroundingUndeclared }

data seed_fold_accumulator_declared_from_an_open_init: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "seed_fold_accumulator_declared_from_an_open_init" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: AwaitsOneGrounding { grounding: GroundingUndeclared }, trigger_capability: "the v2 native compiler emits the closures that contain these folds instead of the v1 seed" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a fold whose init is open (`none`, `[]`, `empty_map()`) and whose step reaches an effect is emitted by the seed as `let mut __fold_acc = None;` with no type, because the effectful loop has no closure for rustc to infer the payload from. HARM: E0282 at cargo build of the emitted crate (gunbc_durable_cas_file_store.rs:510:20, cas_observe_window, calm-crab-645 q-58d6eab), blocking #15310; loud, but only after emission.",
    "REPAIR AT THE BOUNDARY (stated limit, not fixed): the v1 seed has no unifier and mints no type variable, so a nullary generic with no expected type (`none`, `[]`, `empty_map()`) is typed as its bare declaration and the emitter can only leave the accumulator undeclared. v1 is semantics-frozen (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing), so the authored source supplies the type: gunbc.durable_cas_file_store cas_observe_window folds from `init: cas_no_observation()`, a function declared to return CasSlotProbe? (a `let` annotation on the fold result, tried at e047b9835501, does not reach the seed's fold init either: E0282 persisted, observed on srv1). Control: native_emission_controls open_init_fold_declared_result_absent_reads_answer_absent builds the declared form.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1 (mitigatable: loud at rustc, E0282, never silent). CEILING: 3. NEXT TRIGGER (can climb after one grounding): the v2 native compiler emitting these closures instead of the seed. The untyped form is not kept as a fixture: a refusal-expected case cannot share a build with the controls, so the harness for an expected build refusal is the missing piece.",
    "EXECUTED (srv1, calm-crab-645, 1afd2b326ac4): native-emission-controls exit 0 incl. open_init_fold_declared_result_absent_reads_answer_absent; #15310 58d6eab52569 + local merge of 1afd2b3: the cas_observe_window E0282 is gone (the emitted crate then fails elsewhere, unrelated).",
    "RECOGNITION RULE: E0282 `type annotations needed` on `let mut __fold_acc`; source `fold(xs, init: <none|[]|empty_map()>, f: ...)` with an effectful step.",
    "MEMBER, THE E0308 SIDE OF THE SAME GAP (2026-10-31, calm-pike-415). INVALID STATE: `fold(values, init: [], f: fn(acc, v) { if any(acc, e => e == v) { acc } else { append(acc, [v]) } })` -- gunbc.guarantee_measurement distinct_string_count -- emitted its step as `|acc: Rc<Vec<Rc<Vec<String>>>>, v: String|`, so the fold seeded with the empty list was typed a LIST OF LISTS of the receiver's element. HARM: E0308 `mismatched types` twice at that one annotation (the `e == v` comparison against the run, and the `v1_rt::rc_list_concat` of `acc` with the run `[v]`), only at cargo build of the emitted crate. LATENT, NOT A REGRESSION: at main no NativeClaimDriver instrument entry has gunbc.guarantee_measurement in its closure and no emitted mirror of the module is committed, so rustc had never been asked; #15502's gunbc.instruments.router_proxy_falsifier reaches it for the first time, through gunbc.serving.router_dev_policy -> gunbc.serving.serving_layout -> gunbc.repository_census_observation.",
    "REPAIR AT THE LINK (a repair, not the stated limit above): the seed read the open init's element off the step body, and the step body's element came from std.algebra's `append` row, which claims `ReceiverElement` for an argument that the model and the realization BOTH read as either an element OR the whole run -- the interpreter's `method_call.concat` arm merges `value_to_list_carrier(arg)` when the argument is a run and pushes it as one item otherwise, and v1.compiler.emit_rust lowers a list-shaped appended argument to `v1_rt::rc_list_concat` (list ++ list) and only a non-list one to the snoc bridge. `AlgebraTypeTemplate` now carries `ReceiverElementOrSelf` for that dual position and v1.compiler.infer_types `unify_template` decides which form a call is by the ARGUMENT'S OWN type, through `type_is_ordered_element_run` -- the one predicate v1.compiler.emit_rust `type_node_is_ordered_element_run` had already decided once for its two consumers and now shares with inference. `list_push`, FreeMonoid's declared home for a snoc, keeps `ReceiverElement`, so the single-item form is typed exactly as before and nothing outside the defect class (a dual position whose argument is a run, whose receiver is still open) changes.",
    "WHAT REMAINS OPEN IN THIS CLASS: the E0282 member above is untouched -- an effectful step still leaves `let mut __fold_acc` undeclared and the authored source still supplies that type; and inference's string exclusion at a dual position reads only the authored kernel name, so a `FreeMonoid<Char>`-spelled string reaching an OPEN accumulator would still read as a run (the residue is recorded where it is read, v1.compiler.infer_types `type_is_kernel_string`), because inference has no target table of string spellings to consult.",
    "CONTROL, EXECUTED: native_emission_controls `dual_form_append_accumulator_cases` -- six rows, enrolled permanently in `native_emission_expected_identities`. `control_distinct_string_count` is the specimen verbatim; `control_positive_flags` is the sibling that keeps this a RULE rather than an `append` special case: there the accumulator's element is not the receiver's element either, and the run the step appends is again the only place that element type is written down. RED BEFORE the repair at rustc (E0308 in the emitted instrument closure), HELD after; the instrument emits the module itself, so this member needs none of the refusal-expected fixture the E0282 member is missing.",
    "RECOGNITION RULE, E0308 SIDE: a fold closure parameter annotated `Rc<Vec<Rc<Vec<T>>>>` where the receiver is `Rc<Vec<T>>`, from `fold(xs, init: [], f: ...)` whose step appends `append(acc, [<one item>])`; the seed's own append lowering is right throughout, which is what tells the mis-claim apart from a mis-bridge."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "free_monoid_collection_templates", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_types", decl_name: "unify_template", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer_types", decl_name: "type_is_ordered_element_run", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.instruments.native_emission_controls", decl_name: "control_distinct_string_count", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.instruments.native_emission_controls", decl_name: "control_positive_flags", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
